fc0a2e5414ec39e7d46f08b71e3","position":"1785712561501152001-fd295bd8-3960-4c8e-b0d1-00eee27c8689"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"084d8433db7f68e786c9e216627dba360dd08e48865ca305d6acf8916098b928","event_uuid":"d0ac4e90-5cb8-49ab-b13b-7254fc710c12","position":{"commit_sha":"4283a7b02d5a9a5f1c1518c4b111749b5cc80453","position":"1785713013174881001-d0ac4e90-5cb8-49ab-b13b-7254fc710c12"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a2b220e3fd8a2b3e20e84d3e997a3089ffbe85d618b6467f6d68cbcf3d160c6c","event_uuid":"ec9499d6-b5dc-418a-9b08-504298b9479e","position":{"commit_sha":"324b729647729de803bfe111dbe2970b541596ac","position":"1785713049073485001-ec9499d6-b5dc-418a-9b08-504298b9479e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 4a/4b oracle. Contract: classify.py::classify consumes Jira fields only for terminal-local + PRESENT status; membership suffices for active-bound, missing-local, and unbound-present. RED proof: exact pytest run collected 4 nodes and produced 0 passed / 4 failed. Three unit/format nodes falsely placed key-set terminal cases in would_terminal; the real CLI key-set case returned 1 instead of informational 0. Preconditions, full-payload To Do/Done controls, membership-only controls, report text, JSON envelope, exit codes, and read-only bytes are all asserted. The held-out edge/CLI file was then moved outside the implementation worktree; only test_keyset_snapshot_marks_terminal_status_classification_indeterminate remains visible. Standard-tier implementation worker selected: one production module, but semantic classification and report/exit integration are not transcription-level.","timestamp":1785704721095479001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation evidence before full-suite completion:\n- Initial held-out oracle: 4 selected nodes, 0 passed / 4 failed against the pre-fix implementation. Key-set terminal-local cases were falsely reported as would_terminal, and the CLI returned alerting exit 1.\n- Candidate validation: held-out oracle 4/4 passed; related bridge-fsck files 14/14 passed.\n- Mutation proof: disabling the key-set terminal-status fence made a held-out test fail; restoring the fence returned the oracle green.\n- Revert-first test correction: the CLI reducer creates the established .cache.json artifact, so the read-only assertion was narrowed to ignore that cache. The corrected oracle still remained 0/4 RED against the reverted production implementation.\n- make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; production module 611 LOC (<800).\n- A clean make test rerun is active; final result pending.","timestamp":1785711743743973001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Full-suite gate result: two independent clean `make test` runs each reached 8,906 passed, 31 skipped, 178 deselected and then failed only `tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py::test_success_telemetry_survives_an_empty_usage_dict` (missing captured INFO record). This node is outside the ticket file impact and unrelated to bridge-fsck. It passed immediately in isolation after run 1; after run 2, the complete containing module passed 12/12 and its immediately preceding module plus it passed 21/21. The repeated full-suite-only symptom is an order/global-logging-state baseline defect, not candidate behavior. A4-1 remains unchanged; Gerrit Verified will supply the authoritative clean-run decision.","timestamp":1785712220814663001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local enabled four-pass code review of HEAD~1..HEAD PASS: 0 blocking, 0 advisory; pydantic_ai / claude-opus-4-8, five LLM calls, grounding health ok. Commit 5a321985f8 passed DCO, ticket-trailer, lint, typecheck, and commit-message hooks.","timestamp":1785712561501152001}],"created_at":1785372504831187001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"11b383b9-57bc-48c4-bfa5-f6b3f6d0b4e0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0f4d-a428-5e7f-418f"},{"link_uuid":"038b9d41-4a08-436f-9c65-169135b285a4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0f9f-c015-8303-4319"},{"link_uuid":"277c52e8-f621-4084-a180-0f558dbcfaba","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f84f-9718-6589-40e0"},{"link_uuid":"d0ac4e90-5cb8-49ab-b13b-7254fc710c12","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7422-9319-f817-41dc"},{"link_uuid":"1a55f246-0329-419b-b89b-b07fe03536e9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9988-8749-4080-4e10"}],"description":"`bridge_fsck` reads `prev_snapshot.json` off disk as its offline Jira oracle and uses the **field\nvalues**, so narrowing prev to a key-set (A4-2) would silently degrade its drift classification.\nFence it first. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why first\n`bridge_fsck.py:306-308` loads the file as `jira_snapshot` and passes `fields=jira_snapshot[key]`\ninto `ObservedJira.PRESENT` at `:344` and `:380`. With `{}` entries, membership still works but\nevery field-based classification degrades. This is an **out-of-band consumer of the file itself**, not\nof `ctx.prev_snapshot`, so no test that exercises `reconcile_once` would catch it. It reads the\n**working tree**, so it is unaffected by clone filters.\n\n## Approach\nMake the field-dependence explicit: classify on membership where that is sufficient, and where a\nfield value is genuinely required, report the classification as **indeterminate** rather than\ninferring from an empty dict. Do not silently treat absent fields as absent values.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Against a **key-set** prev fixture (`{jira_key: {}}`), `bridge_fsck` drift classification is\n      identical to its classification against the equivalent full-payload fixture for every case that\n      does not require a field value, and reports **indeterminate** (never a false drift) for cases\n      that do. Tier: **unit** with paired fixtures.\n- [ ] Against a full-payload prev, behaviour is byte-identical to today (no regression for the\n      pre-A4-2 world). Tier: **unit** golden comparison.\n- [ ] `rebar bridge-fsck` exit code and JSON shape are unchanged for both fixtures. Tier: **CLI\n      subprocess**.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py`, tests\n\nScope: S. No dependencies (independent of A1/A2/A3).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py","reason":"fence terminal-local classification when a key-set snapshot lacks Jira status"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json","reason":"catalog the additive informational indeterminate drift bucket in the published JSON contract"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_binding_drift.py","reason":"visible unit and schema-contract coverage for key-set terminal classification"},{"path":"tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_fsck_keyset_prev_heldout.py","reason":"held-out paired-fixture, membership, report, JSON-envelope, exit-code, and read-only oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","0f4d-a428-5e7f-418f"],["relates_to","0f9f-c015-8303-4319"],["relates_to","7422-9319-f817-41dc"],["relates_to","9988-8749-4080-4e10"],["relates_to","f84f-9718-6589-40e0"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"99cf9b8d-6cdd-4c75-9703-f6881aee827c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4e3e-d36f-53b9-4c1e","ticket_type":"story","title":"A4-1: fence bridge_fsck's offline drift oracle before prev_snapshot is narrowed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["3f93d46d-93bc-4639-8fa2-7987a1a58957","3b0b3bfc-4cb3-4adf-9106-6de69a7bc3de","1d2edc6e-d89a-4ffb-9e88-eba0590f3f2b","99cf9b8d-6cdd-4c75-9703-f6881aee827c","dc285e20-b2c0-4ca6-aadd-099bbde66251","76830860-401e-4a9b-b398-b97352e005a5","f87446ab-6719-4269-9fc6-eeb5e7368ad8","11b383b9-57bc-48c4-bfa5-f6b3f6d0b4e0","c566ee70-5ca6-4525-8a59-256b4cdcaede","f72ea1c2-0d06-4e0c-8c6e-fdc1d5eedc02","038b9d41-4a08-436f-9c65-169135b285a4","fd295bd8-3960-4c8e-b0d1-00eee27c8689","277c52e8-f621-4084-a180-0f558dbcfaba","d0ac4e90-5cb8-49ab-b13b-7254fc710c12","ec9499d6-b5dc-418a-9b08-504298b9479e","1a55f246-0329-419b-b89b-b07fe03536e9"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785714274637174566,"uuid":"904cd8c1-1451-4050-9ffa-23852a8efe1a"}